# Bifrost SLOs

Performance targets for the Bifrost OLAP warehouse. All numbers below are `TBD (pending bench:bifrost)`. They will be replaced with verified figures from the `bench:bifrost` criterion suite once that suite runs against a named, fixed hardware profile.

> **No performance number ships in this doc unless a verified bench run produced it.** The benchmark suite backing these figures is authored in the consolidated bench pass. Do not replace these placeholders with estimates.

## Architecture-aligned expectations

These are the shapes of the numbers to expect, not committed SLOs. Use them to sanity-check whether observed behavior is broken or working as designed. The `bench:bifrost` suite will produce actual figures.

| Stage | Expected shape | Bound |
|---|---|---|
| Write ack (Gate → Scribe → WAL fsync → ack) | Single-digit milliseconds | fsync latency of the Scribe local disk |
| Seal to Parquet (memtable → object store → `vala.file_list` INSERT) | ~1-5s typical | Time-based seal trigger (1s) + object store PUT + Postgres commit |
| Query freshness (write ack → visible to Oracle) | Within seal latency | Same as seal to Parquet, until live-tail RPC lands |
| Forge compaction lag | TBD | Forge not yet implemented; tick cadence undefined |

**Backpressure boundary:** When seal is stalled (object store slow, Postgres slow), new appends return `429_INGEST_BUSY` rather than growing WAL unboundedly. Watch this counter in production. Sustained rejections mean seal cannot keep up with ingest.

