## Benchmark methodology

When the `bench:bifrost` suite runs:

1. A fixed hardware profile is recorded (CPU, RAM, storage IOPS) and pinned to this page.
2. Each benchmark is run via `mise run bench:bifrost` which emits a machine-readable JSON summary.
3. The p50/p95 figures from that summary replace the `TBD` placeholders here.
4. The hardware profile + run timestamp are cited alongside each figure.

The suite does not run in `pre-pr`; benchmarks are not a correctness gate. The SLO figures are refreshed deliberately when a performance-relevant change lands.

## Benchmark suite (spec, not yet authored)

The following benchmarks will be authored in `crates/vala/vala-bifrost/benches/` as part of the consolidated bench pass:

| Benchmark | Measures |
|---|---|
| `write_insert` | `observe.record` / producer `insert()` call latency |
| `batch_build` | Arrow batch build throughput at the flush boundary |
| `ingest_lag` | End-to-end append → queryable lag |
| `read_get_trace` | `GetTrace` point-lookup latency |
| `read_recent_traces` | `QueryRecentTraces` derived-list latency (includes the in-Rust GROUP-BY) |
| `scan_aggregate` | Aggregation scan throughput over a bounded partition window |
